%N A396229 Number of fixed-content bracelets of length 2*n, summed over all integer partitions of 2*n, whose cyclic orbit contains exactly two linear-palindrome representatives and has full rotational period.
%C A396229 For an integer partition lambda = (lambda_1, ..., lambda_k) of 2*n, use k colors and require color i to occur lambda_i times. The profile lambda is fixed in weakly decreasing order; color relabelings are not additional objects for the same lambda. This is the strongly normal fixed-content convention.
%C A396229 This sequence counts bracelets represented by a circular word X such that (1) the mirror image of X is a rotation of X, (2) exactly two distinct rotations of X are linear palindromes, and (3) no non-identity rotation fixes X. Equivalently, this is the full-period S2 class in the refined fixed-content bracelet atlas.
%C A396229 Let P(2*m) be the total number of strongly normal linear palindromes of length 2*m. A palindrome of even length is determined by its first half, so P(2*m)=A005651(m). The S1 class at even length 2*m is entirely periodic and is counted by A396085(2*m). Therefore H(m) = (A005651(m)-A396085(2*m))/2 counts all S2 cyclic orbits of length 2*m: each such orbit contains two linear-palindrome representatives. Möbius inversion over the rotational period gives the formula below.
%C A396229 The class vanishes in odd underlying length, so the sequence is indexed by half-length n.
%H A396229 Andrea Cutri, <a href="/A396229/b396229.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..40</a>
%H A396229 Andrea Cutri, <a href="https://github.com/aku-79/oeis-refined-atlas/blob/main/programs/a396229.py">Python program</a>.
%F A396229 a(n) = (1/2) * Sum_{d | n} mu(n/d) * (A005651(d) - A396085(2*d)), where mu is the Moebius function.
%e A396229 For n=2 the underlying length is 4. The profile [2,2] gives the single counted bracelet, represented by 0011. Its rotations 0110 and 1001 are the two linear palindromes in the cyclic orbit, and the word has full rotational period 4. Hence a(2)=1.
%e A396229 For n=3, A005651(3)=10 and A396085(6)=2, while the divisor d=1 contributes zero. Thus a(3)=(10-2)/2=4.
%Y A396229 Cf. A005651, A072605, A213943, A395436, A396085, A396630, A396631, A396632.
%K A396229 nonn
%O A396229 2,2
